==Passive effect==
<!--[[File:Chambers of Xeric (10).png|thumb|350px|A graph that shows the accuracy and damage modifiers at different Magic levels. Note that the "buff %" is not an {{wp|Percentage#Percentage_increase_and_decrease|increase}}: at 100%, the accuracy and damage are normal rather than doubled.]]-->
Unlike other bows that have a set strength, the twisted bow functions differently: the higher the target's [[Magic]] level or Magic accuracy is (whichever is higher), the higher the bow's accuracy and damage. The accuracy multiplier caps at 140% (reached at 244 magic level or accuracy), while the damage multiplier caps at 250% (never reached due to the scaling cap).{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Kieren|url=https://twitter.com/JagexKieren/status/869214311675285505|date=29 May 2017|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/104081|archivedate=29 May 2020|quote=Outside raids, magic cap at 250 Acc modifier: 140 + (10 * 3 Magic / 10 - 10) / 100 - ((3 Magic / 10 - 100) ^2) / 100 Capped at 140.}}{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Kieren|url=https://twitter.com/JagexKieren/status/869214343283564544|date=29 May 2017|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/103109|archivedate=29 May 2020|quote=Dmg modifier: 250 + (10 * 3 Magic / 10 - 14) / 100 - ((3 Magic / 10 - 140) ^2) / 100 Capped at 250.}} The Magic level or magic accuracy bonus caps at 250 outside the [[Chambers of Xeric]], and 350 within.

<math>\begin{align}
\text{Accuracy} &= 140 + \frac{\frac{10 \cdot 3 \cdot \text{Magic}}{10} - 10}{100} - \frac{\left(\frac{3 \cdot \text{Magic}}{10} - 100\right)^2}{100} \% & \text{Accuracy} \in [0, 140]\\
\text{Damage} &= 250 + \frac{\frac{10 \cdot 3 \cdot \text{Magic}}{10} - 14}{100} - \frac{\left(\frac{3 \cdot \text{Magic}}{10} - 140\right)^2}{100} \% & \text{Damage} \in [0, 250]
\end{align}</math>
<!--
