==Trivia==
*In {{UD|QoL and CoX Changes|an update}} on [[28 February]] [[2019]], a twisted bow spawn [[Twisted bow glitch|was accidentally added]] east of the [[Farming Guild]]. The spawn was hotfixed shortly after the update{{CiteTwitter|author=Old School RuneScape|url=https://twitter.com/OldSchoolRS/status/1101090319431581698|date=28 February 2019|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/96837|archivedate=28 February 2019|quote=A bug involving Twisted Bows and the Farming guild has been hotfixed. Stand by while we assess our next steps. If you have acquired a Twisted Bows from anywhere other than Chambers of Xeric, they will be removed - attempting to sell them may result in action against your account.}} and the game was [[rollback|rolled back]] to the time of the update.{{CiteNews|url=http://services.runescape.com/m=news/bug-twisted-bows?oldschool=1|newsdate=28 February 2019|author=The Old School Team|title=Bug: Twisted Bows}}
*The twisted bow is similar in function to the [[RSW:Hexhunter bow|Hexhunter bow]] in ''[[RSW:RuneScape|RuneScape 3]]''.
*The ranger [[Mercenary (Theatre of Blood)|mercenary]] outside [[Theatre of Blood]] wields a twisted bow, and it can be seen in one of the webs hanging in [[Nylocas Vasilias]]' room along with its owner. However, this particular bow is a piece of scenery rather than an item. Examining it results in the message {{Mes|It seems like the owner must've dropped it, how unfortunate!}}.
*Upon release, attempting to light a fire after completing [[Barbarian Training|Barbarian Firemaking Training]] resulted in the message {{Mes|Nothing interesting happens.}}. With the release of the [[Inferno]], the message displayed will now state {{Mes|It'd be foolish to possibly damage such an expensive bow with a firemaking attempt. You're surprised you only realised this now!}}.
*As a result of the twisted bow's introduction, [[General Graardor]]'s magic level and magic defence bonus were adjusted as the bow originally outperformed other high-end weapons against him.

